feat: edit your own most recent message from the composer (0.3.0)

The AI-side buttons already render immediately to the right of the copy icon:
the host composes that row as [clock] copy, extraActions, branch, and passes our
slot content as extraActions.

The user row has no such seat. This DSH build exposes only four
conversation.chat.* slots (node, commandview, turnTail, assistant-actions), and
UserMessageNodeView renders MessageIconActions without extraActions and renders
no slot inside the bubble, so a plugin cannot add a control there. Your own
message is therefore edited from the composer, where the slot contract puts
clickable controls:

- conversation.input.left : a small "Edit mine" button in the composer tool row
- conversation.input.dock : the full-width editor above the card
- GET /last-user          : read-only route feeding that control; it skips
                            injected user/message context (source.kind != user)
- lastUserNode()          : the selection rule, covered by unit tests

Saving rewrites the model-visible text only - nothing is sent, no new turn is
started, and the next model request reads the edited text.

Version 0.3.0; CHANGELOG and both READMEs document the split and why.
